  "Interpretation": "On this quiet E1M1 no-input workload, 16 and 20 workers tie at about 48.5 completed headless host render updates/sec; 16 uses about 0.84 GiB less in the end-run combined process working-set sample. Eight workers reduce memory but complete fewer updates. ColorState lowers the slowest-worker median encoding stage from 3.07 ms to 2.63 ms versus the single Pairs-16 sample, while render and decode medians rise slightly; total completed update rate is slightly lower (48.23 vs 48.48/sec). Keep 16 workers and Pairs defaults. These are one ordered screen per setting, not randomized repeats.",
  "Limitations": "Headless output skips ANSI terminal writes, and no process-present or monitor-present frames are measured. This no-input E1M1 check does not qualify route completion, other maps, moving combat, full-session audio, audible quality, or 35-tic/60-display performance. Audio queue starvation is polled software telemetry; canceled queued frames are an exit-tail upper bound, not evidence of mid-session dropouts.",
